From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:20:40 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add CBM core - registers, buffer pools, FSQM

Start the CBM (Central Buffer Manager, the GRX500 "CQM" complex)
support with its foundations:

 - cbm.h / cbm_regs.h: byte-exact structure layouts and the
   register topology of the twelve CBM MMIO windows (EQM enqueue
   manager, DQM dequeue manager, FSQM free-segment queue manager,
   load spreader, descriptor windows, TMU), plus the buffer-pool
   API types (lantiq_cbm_api.h, include/net/cqm_cbm_api.h).

 - cbm_buf.c: the packet-buffer pool allocator. The standard
   (18 MiB) and jumbo (8 MiB) pools are served from no-map
   reserved-memory carve-outs declared in the board DT and mapped
   with memremap; small allocations fall back to the buddy
   allocator. Pool physical bases feed both the FSQM seeding and
   the SBA/JBA base registers.

 - fsqm.c: FSQM initialization - seed the linked-list table
   (LLT_RAM) with the per-slot reference counts, program the
   OFSQ/OFSC/LSARNG free-queue geometry and FSQT thresholds,
   enable interrupts, and only then set CTRL=1. The vendor
   ordering (drain the IO_BUF, arm CTRL last) is load-bearing:
   arming the FSQM before the rest of the geometry is programmed
   corrupts the free-segment accounting.

 - cbm_basic.c: word-wise MMIO helpers and the EQM/DQM counter
   mode configuration (packet vs byte counting with the required
   queue-enable toggle dance), soft-failing before the CBM has
   probed.

Structure layouts and register sequences derived from the AVM
FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198), cqm/grx500/ (cbm.c,
cbm.h, the generated reg/*.h). Those vendor sources carry no
copyright notice of their own, in that release or in any other
checked, so there is none to preserve and none is invented: each
file header names the vendor file it came from instead. The pool
allocator is new for this port.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

